<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico to drain 7.483 bln pesos.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico to drain 7.483 bln pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico sought to drain 7.483 billion pesos from the secondary market on Monday through repurchase agreements and the direct sale of paper, dealers said.</p>
<p>The terms and maturities for the direct sale of Cetes were as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM</p>
<p>    200 million    346 days</p>
<p>    200 million    178 days</p>
<p>    200 million     87 days</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were as follows:</p>
<p>    700 million     39 days</p>
<p>    800 million     38 days</p>
<p>    850 million     35 days</p>
<p>    750 million     31 days</p>
<p>    690 million     24 days</p>
<p>    600 million     23 days</p>
<p>    1.1 bln     17 days</p>
<p>    1.0 bln	9 days</p>
<p>    393 million	1 day</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>((--Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
